# Tenkai local setup — TEMPLATE (tracked on purpose: it carries placeholders only).
#
# Copy this file to .local/tenkai.local.env in the same directory and uncomment the
# four keys with YOUR values. The real file stays untracked: the public
# repository must not name anyone's previous shell (docs/PUBLISH-NOTES.md).
#
# Every reader of the real file — ./tenkai start --fallback, ./tenkai live-stop, the
# full profile's preflight message, ./tenkai live-status and
# docs/revert-to-previous-shell.sh — treats a missing key, an empty value or a
# commented line as "not configured": it says so and does nothing. Nothing is
# ever guessed, and no tracked file carries a start/stop command.
#
# The format is one KEY=value per line (an optional surrounding quote pair is
# stripped); everything else, including these comments, is ignored.
#
# TENKAI_PREV_SHELL_NAME=<the name ./tenkai prints for your previous shell>
# TENKAI_PREV_SHELL_START=<one-line command that starts it — eval'd verbatim, so it must be exact>
# TENKAI_PREV_SHELL_STOP=<one-line command that stops it — printed for you to paste, never run by ./tenkai>
# TENKAI_PREV_SHELL_PROC=<extra process pattern for the watch, e.g. name-a|name-b>
